{
  "_comment": [
    "Example Claude Code settings for running LEGEND end-to-end.",
    "Copy to .claude/settings.local.json and adapt to your machine.",
    "It is an EXAMPLE on purpose: it ships the *shape* of the autonomy contract",
    "(see .claude/skills/legend/SKILL.md), not one machine's paths.",
    "",
    "Why it matters: the autopilot can keep running across the explicitly approved",
    "operations below while the operator is away. Unlisted actions still require",
    "review, so expand the allow-list only after inspecting the exact command.",
    "",
    "SECURITY: this template deliberately does not enable 'bypassPermissions'. That",
    "mode ignores the allow-list and is appropriate only inside an isolated container",
    "or VM. Never run an autonomous session with credentials or identifiable clinical",
    "material in scope. Paid or network services are never auto-authorized: the skills",
    "stop and ask for those."
  ],

  "permissions": {
    "defaultMode": "default",

    "allow": [
      "Read",
      "Write",
      "Edit",

      "Bash(python3 framework/scripts/legend_lint.py *)",
      "Bash(python3 framework/scripts/batch_commit.py *)",
      "Bash(python3 framework/scripts/unread_gold.py *)",
      "Bash(python3 framework/scripts/generate_semantic_graph.py *)",
      "Bash(python3 scripts/public_release_gate.py *)",
      "Bash(python3 scripts/run_release_regressions.py *)",
      "Bash(python3 .claude/skills/legend-study-intake-triage/scripts/*)",
      "Bash(python3 .claude/skills/legend-batch-inferential-sweep/scripts/*)",
      "Bash(python3 .claude/skills/legend-proband-priority-matrix/scripts/*)",
      "Bash(python3 .claude/skills/legend-hypothesis-forge/scripts/*)",
      "Bash(python3 disease-models/*/analysis/scripts/*)",

      "Bash(mkdir -p *)",
      "Bash(cp *)",
      "Bash(ls *)",
      "Bash(find . *)",
      "Bash(git add *)",
      "Bash(git commit -m *)",
      "Bash(git status)",
      "Bash(git diff *)",

      "Bash(python3 -m venv *)"
    ],

    "_comment_mcp": [
      "MCP connectors are optional. PubMed is the one the intake/scout skills use;",
      "authorize it in your own client. Nothing in this repository requires it to run",
      "the LINT, the release gate, or the analysis pipeline."
    ],
    "allowMcp": [
      "mcp__PubMed__search_articles",
      "mcp__PubMed__get_article_metadata",
      "mcp__PubMed__get_full_text_article",
      "mcp__PubMed__convert_article_ids"
    ]
  }
}
